{"name":"Chartreuse Shot","hex":"#dad000","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"chartreuse","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A yellow or green liqueur made by Carthusian monks.","A greenish-yellow color."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a bright yellowish-green colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chartreuse"},{"term":"shot","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Tired, weary.","Discharged, cleared, or rid of something."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of shoot"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shot"}],"entries":[{"title":"Chartreuse (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Chartreuse is a color between yellow and green also referred to as yellow-green or greenish yellow. It was named because of its resemblance to the French liqueur green chartreuse, introduced in 1764. Similarly, chartreuse yellow is a yellow color mixed with a small amount of green, named after the drink yellow chartreuse. The wavelength and frequency of chartreuse is near 547.5 nm or 547.5 THz."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/RAF-Cardington-Shed02_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-RAF-Cardington-Shed02_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chartreuse_(color)","wikidata":"Q1153119"},{"title":"Chartreuse (liqueur)","blocks":[{"text":"Chartreuse is a French herbal liqueur that has been made by Carthusian monks since 1737, reportedly according to instructions set out in a manuscript given to them by François Annibal d'Estrées in 1605. It was named after the monks' Grande Chartreuse monastery, located in the Chartreuse Mountains north of Grenoble, France. Today the liqueur is produced in their distillery in nearby Aiguenoire. It is composed of distilled alcohol aged with 130 herbs, plants and flowers, and sweetened, though the exact recipe is known only to select monks. The color chartreuse takes its name from the drink."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Schnapsglas_gr%C3%BCner_Chartreuse.jpg/330px-Schnapsglas_gr%C3%BCner_Chartreuse.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chartreuse_(liqueur)","wikidata":"Q779839"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Catopsilia_pomona_by_kadavoor.JPG/500px-Catopsilia_pomona_by_kadavoor.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Catopsilia_pomona_by_kadavoor.JPG/1280px-Catopsilia_pomona_by_kadavoor.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Catopsilia_pomona_by_kadavoor.JPG/500px-Catopsilia_pomona_by_kadavoor.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACatopsilia_pomona_by_kadavoor.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/Henry_Prince_of_Wales_on_the_Hunting_Field_Robert_Peake.jpg/500px-Henry_Prince_of_Wales_on_the_Hunting_Field_Robert_Peake.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/Henry_Prince_of_Wales_on_the_Hunting_Field_Robert_Peake.jpg/1280px-Henry_Prince_of_Wales_on_the_Hunting_Field_Robert_Peake.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/Henry_Prince_of_Wales_on_the_Hunting_Field_Robert_Peake.jpg/500px-Henry_Prince_of_Wales_on_the_Hunting_Field_Robert_Peake.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHenry_Prince_of_Wales_on_the_Hunting_Field_Robert_Peake.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://t